# offsets.map -- what each entry of the off:: namespace in src/game/game_syms.h IS.
#
#   <constant>            <Class::member>     the PDB must agree this member is at that offset
#   <constant>            -                   deliberately NOT a struct offset: a stride, an enum
#                                             value, an index, or a field of a type the PDB does not
#                                             name. Recorded so it reads as decided, not forgotten.
#
# Lines here are DATA for omp_offcheck; the mod does not read this file and does not build against
# it. Nothing in it can change how the mod behaves.
#
# An entry is only worth adding if the class is the one the CODE dereferences. A member that merely
# happens to sit at the same offset will agree with the PDB today and keep agreeing after the field
# it was supposed to be watching has moved -- which is worse than leaving the offset unmapped.
# offcheck.py --discover only proposes what a comment already names, for exactly that reason.

